.TH SUFFIX 1 2026-07-17 "Suffix 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
suffix \- manage durable short links on domains you own
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B suffix
.RI [ command ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B suffix man install
.RI [ --dir " man1-directory" ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B suffix
is the command-line client for the Suffix canonical API at
.B https://suffix.org/api/v1.
It manages only the domains and shortcuts belonging to the active saved account.
Use
.B suffix login
to approve and store a bearer key through the browser.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B login [email]
Open a browser login flow and save a one-time API key. The optional email is a
sign-in hint.
.TP
.B ls [--json|--yaml|--xml] [-l|--stats]
List shortcuts. The normal output is tab-separated shortcut and destination
columns.
.TP
.B add [options] \fIvalue\fR [\fItail\fR] [\fItarget-url\fR]
Create a shortcut. Use a hostname-and-tail value such as
.B pair.rs/typesec
or use
.B -d
with an explicit domain hostname.
.TP
.B rm \fIshortcut-id\fR [--version \fIversion\fR]
Delete a shortcut. If no version is supplied, Suffix reads it before deleting.
.TP
.B domain ls|add|rm
List, add, or remove owned domains.
.TP
.B transfer \fIdomain\fR [--to \fIemail\fR]
Create a short-lived code for moving a domain to another account.
.TP
.B accept \fIcode\fR
Accept a domain-transfer code into the active account.
.TP
.B account [ls|add|rm|name]
List, add, remove, or select saved account profiles.
.TP
.B man install [--dir \fIman1-directory\fR]
Install this manual as
.I suffix.1
in the first writable standard section-1 manual directory. On macOS, Suffix
checks Homebrew, local, and user-local directories. On Linux, it checks local,
user-local, and system directories. Use
.B --dir
to select an exact directory. A system-owned destination may require elevated
privileges.
.SH FILES
.TP
.B suffix/config.toml
The platform configuration directory holds saved API bases, account metadata,
and API keys.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SUFFIX_API_BASE
Overrides the saved API base URL.
.TP
.B SUFFIX_API_KEY
Overrides the saved bearer API key.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B suffix
exits zero on success and nonzero for invalid arguments or authentication,
API, and manual-page installation failures.
.SH SEE ALSO
The Suffix dashboard and API documentation are available at
.B https://suffix.org.
